Open Vanilla 0024: Duels in Gurubashi Arena, the hangout, spectating, sudden death and Glicko-2 (on top of 0010 and 0021).

Every setting is off unless the Duels realm sets it (hetzner/duels_up.sh), so Warfront and the live realm
are unchanged:
- OpenVanilla.Duels.Arena = gurubashi: matches in Gurubashi Arena on map 900, a party-instance copy of
  Eastern Kingdoms (tools/duels/arena_map.py writes its Map.dbc row; duels_up.sh links map 0's maps,
  vmaps and mmaps to it and adds the instance_template row). A copy per match, fenced to the pit.
  Without the map in place it says so in the log and stays in the Ring of Law.
- OpenVanilla.Duels.Hub (+ .Hub.Fence): the hangout (the Lion's Pride Inn). Outside a match a duelist
  is kept there, both factions friendly; after a match they come back there, not to where they were.
- OpenVanilla.Duels.AutoQueue = d1: queued from the hangout after a few idle seconds; leaving the queue
  stops it until the next join, "auto off" for good (duels_player.auto_queue).
- watch [id|stop], fights: spectate a duel from the stands, invisible and untouchable; the fights now
  go to duels_now every 15 s for the website.
- OpenVanilla.Duels.SuddenDeathSeconds: from then on in a round, 10% more damage and 15% less healing
  taken per stack, a stack every 15 s (Unit.cpp asks Warfront::Arena::TakenScale).
- OpenVanilla.Duels.Consumables: potions and the like topped up at every round.
- OpenVanilla.Duels.Glicko (on): the duel ladder on Glicko-2 (rd, vol next to the rating), and Duel
  Points per rated duel (earned only, cosmetic only): 25 a win, 5 a loss, 10 more for ending a streak.
Owner, 2026-10-21: "built the whole thing, gurubashi and future spectate mode".

